{
  "format": "zapterm-command-lists",
  "version": 1,
  "platform": "cisco_iosxr",
  "notes": "Cisco IOS XR command lists. Every command below was checked against Cisco's IOS XR command references (command syntax or a documented example) — nothing was added from memory: • Cisco 8000: BGP, Routing, MPLS and System Setup command references • ASR 9000: General Administration, System Setup, Interface and Hardware Component, IP Addresses and Services, Routing, System Security, System Management, System Monitoring, Advanced System and L2VPN command references • NCS 5500: Interfaces, System Monitoring, System Management and System Security command references Left out: debug/undebug commands (not found in those references), commands that reload or erase the device, and ones not found there.",
  "label": "Cisco IOS XR",
  "stopDebug": [],
  "lists": [
    {
